\fs24\lang4105\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp4105\langfenp1033 {\f2\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033 I created these campaigns sometime in 1998-99
, but now it's 2003 and 4 years later.  I find it amazing that Netstorm has managed to hold on despite the fallings of Titanic Entertainment and sometime after Activision as well.
\par 
\par I still believe Netstorm to be an ideal RTS game, one of the few perhaps under the right circumstances.  It can be a game of strategy as opposed to massing a cookie cutter army after a cookie cutter build order like so many others.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri262\nowidctlpar\tx8378\tx8662\faauto\rin262\lin0\itap0 {\f2\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\langnp1033 
\par Before I left Netstorm I did have a campaign more or less completed, but never truly released.  It was an experiment to try and integrate a sacrifice system into the single player mode.  Though I did complete the system the test campaign I integrated it 
into wasn't all that interesting, as was my interest in Netstorm at the time.
\par 
\par I've added 'cheat' options to my campaigns, which will basically allow you to play all the missions without the hassle of actually defeating the missions all in order.  This should be a relief to whoever has ever played "The New Ruler of Nimbus" 
campaign that for all intents and purposes is extremely hard.
\par 
\par Thus I bring you my old new campaign, "The Trials of Priesthood". 
\par 
\par If you have any questions or comments feel free to e-mail me at rahn45@hotmail.com or visit the comic site I now maintain at http://shallow.keenspace.com or my art gallery at http://bladewing.deviantart.com/
\par 
\par -Adley Tang (Aka: Rahn)
